    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The radii of the three concentric circles shown, are 2, 4 and 6 respectively. The diameters cut each circle into quarters. What is the area of the shaded region?",
    "image": "qimages/samf/senior-2017-r1/q02.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$8\\pi$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$12\\pi$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$16\\pi$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$18\\pi$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$24\\pi$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Half the big circle",
        "body": "Rotating the middle ring by $90^\\circ$ shows that the shaded parts of each ring fill exactly half of it. So the shaded region is half of the largest circle: $\\frac12\\pi\\cdot6^2=18\\pi$.\n\n**Answer: (D) $18\\pi$**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Add the ring areas",
        "body": "In each of the three regions (inner disc, middle ring, outer ring) two opposite quarters are shaded, i.e. half of its area: $\\frac12\\pi\\cdot2^2+\\frac12\\pi(4^2-2^2)+\\frac12\\pi(6^2-4^2)=2\\pi+6\\pi+10\\pi=18\\pi$.\n\n**Answer: (D) $18\\pi$**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "geometry"
    ],
    "difficulty": 2,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
  },
