        "key": "C",
        "text": "It cannot be in the third quadrant"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "It cannot be in the fourth quadrant"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "It can be in any quadrant"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Sign analysis",
        "body": "The point lies on the line $x+y=2$. In the third quadrant $x<0$ and $y<0$, so $x+y<0\\ne2$. The line passes through quadrants I (e.g. $(1;1)$), II ($(-1;3)$) and IV ($(3;-1)$).\n\n**Answer: (C)**"
      }
    ],
