        "body": "$AD=BC=12$. In triangle $ADE$ the angles at $A$ and $D$ are $60^\\circ$ (since $\\angle BAE=\\angle CDE=30^\\circ$ and $\\angle BAD=\\angle CDA=90^\\circ$), so $ADE$ is equilateral with side $12$ and $AE=ED=12$. The perimeter is $AB+BC+CD+DE+EA=12\\cdot5=60$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 60**"
