    "prompt": "The floor of a real number $x$, denoted by $\\lfloor x\\rfloor$, is the largest integer less than or equal to the number, e.g. $\\lfloor3.2\\rfloor=3$. The ceiling of a real number $x$, denoted by $\\lceil x\\rceil$, is the smallest integer greater than or equal to the number, e.g. $\\lceil-4.7\\rceil=-4$. What is the value of $\\lceil\\sqrt{23}\\rceil+\\lfloor-3.2\\rfloor$?",
