        "text": "61"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Digit inequality",
        "body": "Write $n=10a+b$ ($1\\le a\\le9$, $0\\le b\\le9$). Then $10a+b>8(a+b)$ gives $2a>7b$. Since $2a\\le18$, $b\\le2$. $b=0$: $a=1,\\dots,9$ ($9$ values). $b=1$: $2a>7$, $a=4,\\dots,9$ ($6$ values). $b=2$: $2a>14$, $a=8,9$ ($2$ values). Total $9+6+2=17$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 17**"
